Grandma’s Story: The Half Roti (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100154

Grandma smiled and said, “This one is about kindness.”

“Long ago, a poor boy was walking home, very hungry.

He had only one roti in his hand.

As he walked, he saw an even poorer old man sitting by the road.

The old man looked weak and hungry.

The boy stopped.

He looked at his roti… and then at the old man.

Slowly, he broke the roti into two halves.

He gave one half to the old man.

The old man ate and smiled.

‘May you never stay hungry,’ he blessed.

Years later, the boy grew up and became successful.

Grandma said, ‘Kindness always comes back, in ways we don’t expect.’”

💖 Moral:

Sharing with others brings blessings.
